# Frontend scope (token)

When the task is under `frontend/`, stay there unless the user asks for API or DB changes.

## Stay in-stack

- Prefer: page/component → existing hooks/API modules → shared UI patterns in the same area (`Campus/`, `Academics/`, `employee/`).
- Do **not** open `backend/` to rediscover routes/DTOs if the frontend API client or types already show the contract.
- Employee Portal (`components/employee/`): mobile-first only — do not pull desktop Campus admin patterns “for reference” unless needed.

## Cheap lookups

- Copy density/spacing/copy tone from a sibling page in the same folder; do not re-read `index.css` + Students list unless changing table/chrome styles.
- Reuse existing axios/fetch helpers; do not invent new HTTP clients.
- No `PUT` — use POST update routes already used by nearby screens.
- User-facing copy: plain staff language; no developer jargon (no FundType IDs, “null”, “skipped”, table names).
